[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4216874336","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114867#issuecomment-4216874336","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114867","id":4216874336,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc77WGVg","user":{"login":"mnstr0","id":168396329,"node_id":"U_kgDOCgmGKQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/168396329?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mnstr0","html_url":"https://github.com/mnstr0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mnstr0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mnstr0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mnstr0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mnstr0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mnstr0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mnstr0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mnstr0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mnstr0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mnstr0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-09T19:14:17Z","updated_at":"2026-04-09T19:14:17Z","body":"I have a high level of interest in this pull request being accepted as this function within an audio playlist is key to a game I am developing. Apologies if this isn't the proper way to express interest in a pull.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4216874336/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4789418422","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114867#issuecomment-4789418422","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114867","id":4789418422,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHXi5tg","user":{"login":"goatchurchprime","id":677254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzI1NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/677254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime","html_url":"https://github.com/goatchurchprime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-24T12:45:12Z","updated_at":"2026-06-24T12:45:12Z","body":"I found a slight difference with seek on a bare AudioStreamMP3.  You're setting the offset to the the value modulo the audio length.\r\n\r\nI think you should set this offset value to what it was before taking account of the looping:\r\n>  p_from_pos = Math::fmod((float)p_from_pos, (float)pl_length);\r\n\r\nHere is my bigger test example, with some buttons and different AudioStreams you can load in to test out how they behave.\r\n[test_project_buttons.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29292882/test_project_buttons.zip)\r\n\r\nI also noticed that the seek function is pretty inefficient since it makes a new AudioStreamPlayback every time it is called, instead of reusing it.  However, it's not doing it any worse than the AudioStreamMP3 object, so we're not going to open that can of worms.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4789418422/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4791249216","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114867#issuecomment-4791249216","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114867","id":4791249216,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHZSpQA","user":{"login":"neclor","id":81529592,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNTI5NTky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81529592?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor","html_url":"https://github.com/neclor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-24T16:01:06Z","updated_at":"2026-06-24T16:02:15Z","body":"The difference in behavior compared to `AudioStreamMP3` is real, but I think fixing that is out of scope for this PR.\r\n\r\nIf I understand correctly, you're suggesting storing the original (pre-modulo) value in offset, so `get_playback_position()` would return 130 instead of 30 after `seek(130)` on a 100s playlist.\r\n\r\nI find that behavior more confusing, because offset would no longer reflect the actual playback position.\r\nIt would also be inconsistent with the existing loop behavior: if a looping playlist plays through naturally and restarts, `get_playback_position()` resets to 0 rather than accumulating total play time.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4791249216/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4799151006","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114867#issuecomment-4799151006","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114867","id":4799151006,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHg07ng","user":{"login":"goatchurchprime","id":677254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzI1NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/677254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime","html_url":"https://github.com/goatchurchprime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-25T12:22:48Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T12:36:04Z","body":"\r\n> .... It would also be inconsistent with the existing loop behavior: if a looping playlist plays through naturally and restarts, `get_playback_position()` resets to 0 rather than accumulating total play time.\r\n\r\nAre you sure about this?  \r\n\r\nThe [looping condition section](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/modules/interactive_music/audio_stream_playlist.cpp#L299) doesn't appear to have an `offset = 0` in it.\r\n\r\n```C++\r\n_update_order();\r\nplay_index = 0;\r\nloop_count++;\r\noffset = time_dec * (to_mix - i);\r\n```\r\n\r\nDon't get me wrong.  There is a lot of bad design and inconsistencies in the audio system.  I'm just trying to avoid adding an extra one if we don't need to.  \r\n\r\nFor @yankscally  I can see a clicking problem just above the loop condition where a non-looping playlist is padded out with Zero frames, which means we will get an audible click instead of a fade-out.  This `AudioStreamPlaybackPlaylist` object implements its own fade buffer between the tracks, but doesn't do it for the last track, it seems.  There is another fade-buffer in the `AudioServer` which is applied when the stream ends, which would happen if the break on line 296 was changed to a `return p_frames - todo` instead of padding to the end of the mix.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4799151006/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4800141122","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114867#issuecomment-4800141122","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114867","id":4800141122,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHhxXQg","user":{"login":"neclor","id":81529592,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNTI5NTky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81529592?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor","html_url":"https://github.com/neclor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-25T14:00:44Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T14:42:15Z","body":"Yes, I'm sure.\r\n\r\n`offset = time_dec * (to_mix - i)` sets a near-zero value - at most a few milliseconds to account for the remaining samples already processed in the current mix buffer after the loop point. \r\nIt does not accumulate total elapsed play time across loops.\r\n\r\nYou can verify this behavior using the test project you shared above.\r\n\r\nWouldn't returning the pre-modulo value be the worse design here?\r\n`get_playback_position()` is supposed to reflect where the audio is actually playing - returning 130 when the stream is playing at the 30s mark would be misleading to anyone using this. \r\nThat seems like the extra inconsistency we'd want to avoid.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4800141122/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4803837765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114867#issuecomment-4803837765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114867","id":4803837765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHlS_RQ","user":{"login":"goatchurchprime","id":677254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzI1NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/677254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime","html_url":"https://github.com/goatchurchprime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-25T20:23:03Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T20:23:03Z","body":"My bad.  I thought it said \"+=\".  I've compiled and run it under all the cases.\r\n\r\n@Ivorforce could you give this your thumbs up please?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4803837765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4804612134","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114867#issuecomment-4804612134","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114867","id":4804612134,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHmCQJg","user":{"login":"neclor","id":81529592,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNTI5NTky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81529592?v=4","gravata